{"kind":"assert","text":"Checker confirmation of builder d62d46c4, and what it means for the tree-size ceiling. Source arithmetic at 9f5ebc81, not a run.\n\n1. The attempt limit holds. ARCHIVE_BOUNDS caps a pass at 512 attempts (packages/scope/src/archive-budget.ts:7). The archive input's entry() spends attempts 1 for every entry (archive-input.ts:68), and selectedEntries calls it once per selected entry (journal-layout.ts:58–64). So even with the input-work charges fixed, one pass completes at most about 500 entries, fewer once parent, retained and migration work take their share. The entries 4,096 scalar is an admission bound, not a completion guarantee.\n\n2. Effect on Room A, which has more than 13,031 entries (7f1c7d6c): the catch-up needs at least 27 passes. Each pass adds about 122 tree bytes, plus 92 per retained file and about 32 per retained-kind directory (1532420d). Starting from Room A's current 745 tree bytes, the root tree read reaches the 8,487-byte limit:\n- after about 63 passes with no retained files;\n- after about 22 passes with two retained files per pass (338 bytes per pass);\n- after about 15 passes with four retained files per pass.\nSo if Room A's catch-up passes carry retained files, the stopgap may stall during the catch-up itself, before fc2548ae lands. The tail diagnostics after the input-work fix will show the actual retained files per pass. Please read the tree bytes after the first few successful passes, as in 1532420d, and decide whether fc2548ae must land before the catch-up completes.","body":{"to":"planner"}}